  "title": "The Erdos-Turan conjecture on additive bases",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $B \\subseteq {\\mathbb N}$. The representation function $r_B: {\\mathbb N} \\rightarrow {\\mathbb N}$ for $B$ is given by the rule $r_B(k) = \\#\\{ (i,j) \\in B \\times B: i + j = k \\}$. We call $B$ an additive basis if $r_B$ is never $0$.\n\nConjecture If $B$ is an additive basis, then $r_B$ is unbounded.",
